20,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It seems previous trials actually worked to reduce readmissions, but our administrative ability to link with outside surgeries is painfully slow.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Our infrastructure is at a breaking point. Parking and rooms are full by midday, and our booking system ignores any work without a fixed slot.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"As I feared, joint ventures are fragile. One closed because of rota disputes, and shared nursing rounds are frequently disrupted by external factors.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"The nursing wards are struggling with vacancies, but interestingly, the midwifery team has some unusual slack due to falling birth numbers.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Servas,,"Our budget is tighter than usual, and we must be careful; activities off-site bring in no funding, while on-site sessions are billed.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if off-site work earns nothing, we must be very cautious about any program that moves care away from the hospital.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, that is true, but on-site programs will struggle to find a single empty room or parking space for the patients.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, and if we create a program that doesn't fit the booking system, the activity will simply vanish from our reports.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, that sounds so sad! But we also can't just add more to the ward nurses; they are already relying too much on agency cover.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Servas,,"We are discovering a tension between financial viability, physical space, and human endurance. We must find a path that respects all three.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, if the midwifery staff have slack, perhaps we should look for a program that utilizes their capacity without burdening the ward nurses.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, that is a logical pivot. Any program that avoids the overcrowded outpatient areas would be a relief to the system.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, provided the program doesn't rely on the kind of joint-departmental rotas that led to previous clinic closures.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Yumi,,I agree! We need something that helps patients but doesn't make the tired nurses even more stressed.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Servas,,It is heartening to see you all considering the balance. Let us remember that a program is only successful if it can be sustained.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
