50,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Looking at the candidates, the Perinatal Support Service seems promising since it uses the midwifery slack Yumi mentioned.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"The Home Follow-Up Team and Chronic Care Coordination avoid our parking and room crisis, but Chronic Care requires those slow data agreements.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The Perinatal service is joint-run, which is a risk. The Day Rehabilitation Unit requires dedicated space, which Toshio says we don't have.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I love the Perinatal Support Service! It uses the midwifery team who have space, and it helps new parents.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The Home Follow-Up Team is noble, but as I found, off-site visits earn no tariffs. The Perinatal service is on-site and billable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the risk of a joint venture is real, but the Perinatal service is the only one that fits our current staffing reality.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, if the Perinatal service is on-site, we must ensure it doesn't seize up the booking system or the car park.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, if it's scheduled as a clinic, it's recorded. But I still worry about the midwifery and pediatric departments fighting over the budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, maybe they won't fight if they know it's the best way to help the families! It feels like the most positive choice.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the risk of friction is always there, but the financial and staffing alignment of the Perinatal service is quite strong.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Asuka,,The Home Follow-Up Team is too risky financially and operationally given the visit completion failures Benjamin found.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I agree. Chronic Care is a bureaucratic nightmare with the data agreements. Perinatal is the most absorbable option.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"If we must choose, the Perinatal service is less likely to fail than a Day Unit with no rooms or a Home team with no funding.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm so happy we're agreeing! Let's go with the Perinatal Support Service!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It seems we have found a harmony between the budget, the staff, and the patients. I am ready to vote.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I vote for the Perinatal Support Service!,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Servas,,I vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
